  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "What is the difference between two coterminal angles?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "An integer multiple of \\(180^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(90^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "They must be equal",
    "D": "An integer multiple of \\(360^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Rotating more or less by a whole number of full revolutions returns the terminal side to the same position. Conversely, with the same initial side, returning to the same terminal side requires a whole number of full revolutions. Thus the difference between coterminal angles is \\(k\\cdot360^\\circ\\), where \\(k\\) is any integer, including zero. D gives this exact characterization.\n\nHowever, \\(k\\cdot360^\\circ=(2k)\\cdot180^\\circ\\), so A also holds for every coterminal pair. A is weaker: \\(0^\\circ\\) and \\(180^\\circ\\) differ by an integer multiple of \\(180^\\circ\\) but have different terminal sides. Therefore A and D are both true as written; D is uniquely intended only if the question asks for an exact characterization.",
